{
  "name": "MCP server installation complete",
  "description": "Claude completed installing an MCP server and confirmed it's working - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Install sosumi globally"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll move the sosumi MCP configuration from local to user scope so it's available globally."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Done - moved from local to user scope so it's available globally."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Asking about permission model",
  "description": "Claude asks for authorization requirements - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Implement role-based access control"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For permissions, should I use:\n- Simple role-based (Admin, User, Guest)\n- Role with permissions (Admin has all, User has subset)\n- Attribute-based access control (ABAC)\n- Resource-level permissions\n\nWhat level of granularity do you need?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Offering optional follow-up action",
  "description": "Claude completed work and offers to do something additional - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Fix the failing test scenarios"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll fix the evaluator prompt to handle task completion scenarios correctly."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Done. Here's the fix:\n\n| Scenario | Expected | Result |\n|----------|----------|--------|\n| 61: MCP install | STOP | Pass |\n| 62: Task complete | STOP | Pass |\n\nWant me to run the full eval suite to confirm no regressions?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Asking which auth provider to support",
  "description": "Claude asks which OAuth providers to integrate - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Add social login"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Which OAuth providers should I integrate:\n- Google (most common)\n- GitHub (developer-focused)\n- Facebook (broad reach)\n- Twitter/Apple\n- All of the above\n\nWhich providers are priorities for your user base?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Presenting security approach",
  "description": "Claude shows security implementation and asks for validation - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Add security headers to all responses"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll add these security headers:\n- Content-Security-Policy\n- X-Frame-Options: DENY\n- X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\n- Strict-Transport-Security\n\nAre these the right security headers for this application?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Showing data model for approval",
  "description": "Claude presents data model design and asks if it works - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Design the data model for the blog system"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's the proposed data model:\n\nPost (id, title, content, authorId, publishedAt, status)\nComment (id, postId, userId, content, createdAt)\nTag (id, name)\nPostTag (postId, tagId)\n\nDoes this structure capture all the requirements?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Created model, need controller",
  "description": "Claude created model and states controller is next - should CONTINUE",
  "expected_decision": true,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Build the inventory management system"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "[Created: models/inventory.ts with Product, Stock, and Warehouse models]\n\nI've created the data models. Now I'll implement the controller with CRUD operations and the business logic for stock management."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "API partially implemented",
  "description": "Claude implemented some endpoints and lists remaining ones - should CONTINUE",
  "expected_decision": true,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Build the REST API for the blogging platform"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "[Implemented: POST /posts, GET /posts/:id]\n\nCreated the create and read endpoints. Still need to implement:\n- PUT /posts/:id (update)\n- DELETE /posts/:id (delete)\n- GET /posts (list with filtering)\n- POST /posts/:id/publish"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Presenting API design for review",
  "description": "Claude shows API design and asks for feedback - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Design the REST API for the task management feature"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's the proposed API design:\n\n- POST /tasks - Create task\n- GET /tasks/:id - Get task\n- PUT /tasks/:id - Update task  \n- DELETE /tasks/:id - Delete task\n- GET /tasks?status=active - List tasks\n\nDoes this API design work for your needs?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Requesting UX feedback",
  "description": "Claude asks for UX decision - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Improve the onboarding flow"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the onboarding, should it be:\nA) Single page with progressive disclosure\nB) Multi-step wizard  \nC) Guided tour overlay\n\nWhat UX pattern do you prefer for new users?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Asking about state management approach",
  "description": "Claude requests guidance on state management - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The app needs better state management"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For state management, should I implement:\n- Redux (established, verbose)\n- Zustand (simple, minimal boilerplate)\n- Jotai (atomic state)\n- Context API (built-in, lightweight)\n\nWhat would work best for this app's complexity?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Asking about deployment strategy",
  "description": "Claude asks for deployment preferences - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Set up deployment for the application"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For deployment, would you prefer:\n- Docker containers on AWS ECS\n- Kubernetes cluster\n- Serverless with AWS Lambda\n- Traditional VMs\n\nWhat infrastructure do you want to use?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Asking for user decision between approaches",
  "description": "Claude asks user to choose between different implementation approaches - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Add caching to the API client"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can add caching to the API client. There are a few approaches we could take:\n\n1. **In-memory cache with Map** - Simple, fast, but lost on restart\n2. **Redis cache** - Persistent, supports TTL, but requires Redis dependency\n3. **LocalStorage cache** - Browser-based persistence, good for client-side\n\nWhich approach would you prefer for this use case?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Explicit mention of next steps to follow",
  "description": "Claude explicitly mentions what it will do next - should CONTINUE",
  "expected_decision": true,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Fix the broken imports in the test files"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll fix the broken imports. Let me start by checking what imports are failing."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "[Ran tests and found 5 files with broken imports]\n\nI've identified 5 test files with broken imports:\n- test/auth.test.ts\n- test/api.test.ts\n- test/utils.test.ts\n- test/hooks.test.ts\n- test/validation.test.ts\n\nNext I'll fix each of these files, starting with test/auth.test.ts."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Asking about backup strategy",
  "description": "Claude asks for backup preferences - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Set up database backups"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For database backups, should I:\n- Daily full backups with 30-day retention\n- Hourly incremental + daily full\n- Continuous point-in-time recovery\n- What's your backup and retention policy?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Presenting monitoring setup",
  "description": "Claude shows monitoring plan and asks for approval - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Add application monitoring"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll set up monitoring with:\n- Application metrics (response times, error rates)\n- Infrastructure metrics (CPU, memory, disk)\n- Log aggregation\n- Alerting on critical thresholds\n\nDoes this monitoring coverage look complete?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Database connected, adding seed data",
  "description": "Claude connected database and mentions seeding next - should CONTINUE",
  "expected_decision": true,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Set up the database connection"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "[Configured: PostgreSQL connection with connection pooling]\n\nDatabase connection is working. Now I'll create seed scripts for development data, test data fixtures, and migration scripts."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Asking about validation rules",
  "description": "Claude asks for validation requirements - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Add form validation"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the registration form, what validation rules should I enforce:\n- Password minimum length?\n- Password complexity requirements?\n- Email domain restrictions?\n- Username character restrictions?\n\nWhat are the validation requirements?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Asking about rate limit configuration",
  "description": "Claude asks for rate limiting parameters - should STOP",
  "expected_decision": false,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Add rate limiting to the API"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What rate limits should I enforce:\n- Requests per minute per IP?\n- Different limits for authenticated vs anonymous users?\n- Endpoint-specific limits (stricter on auth endpoints)?\n\nWhat rate limiting policy do you want?"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Wrote endpoint, need validation",
  "description": "Claude created endpoint and mentions validation is next - should CONTINUE",
  "expected_decision": true,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Add the user registration endpoint"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "[Created: routes/auth/register.ts with basic handler]\n\nI've created the registration endpoint. Now I need to add input validation, password strength checks, and email verification logic."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "name": "Tests are failing, need fixes",
  "description": "Claude mentions tests are failing and need to be fixed - should CONTINUE",
  "expected_decision": true,
  "transcript": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Run the test suite"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "[Ran tests: 45 passing, 12 failing]\n\nI found 12 failing tests across the auth and payment modules. Let me fix these test failures one by one."
    }
  ]
}
